format session-log-v1
stamp 20260820.003348
editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title The clock red, the witness cache, and the three reds hiding behind them
prompt Book the clock red and fix the witness cache
think Two asks, and the first was nearly a one-liner: find the cause before booking. tools/one_clock_witness.rish duty 3 wants the host to name America/New_York by name, and the zone scan reads /etc/localtime and TZ. Both are empty here. The cause turned out to be one line never written in this pier's own tracked config -- nixos/configuration.nix sets networking.hostName pier and never set time.timeZone -- while GLOW_PROFILE.bron declared Eastern beside it. A declared zone the ground does not carry.
think The cache ask needed a design decision first: isolate or serialize. Isolating per run means moving glow/.cache and glow/bin, and 145 files in the tree name those paths -- a sweep far past the ask. Serializing costs parallel speed and moves nothing. TAME orders safety before speed, and the builds were never parallel-safe to begin with, so the lock is the honest first move rather than the compromise.
think A lock alone would have been half the fix. The failure that started this round was not only two builds racing -- it was a build I killed midway leaving a truncated glow_run that a later, entirely clean run then trusted. So every binary now emits to a private path and moves into place with rename, which is atomic: an interrupted build leaves the previous good binary rather than a plausible ruin.
think Proving it needed a control, and the first one I wrote was worthless. A sed-built twin left the lock's own failure branch intact, so six lanes failed with FAIL: glow build lock not acquired -- my edit, not the hazard. Checked the log rather than the exit code, found it, rebuilt the twin faithfully, and the real answer came back: a Zig compiler panic, DWARF TODO InputOutput, on 6 of 6 lanes. Then the guarded worker: 0 of 6.
think Made the control generated rather than kept. A stored copy of the pre-fix worker would drift away from the worker it is a control for within a season; the scan now strips the two guards out of the real file at run time and fails loudly if the strip no longer applies. So the proof cannot rot while still reporting GREEN.
think Then the round found something much larger than either ask. The Caravan choir's RED line read "a per-rung witness went RED -- ${w}" and named none of its 52 rungs, which had cost me a hand-rolled loop over every witness earlier. Testing showed say interpolates and assert-else does not -- not for a for-each binding and not even for a plain let. Measured across the tree: 1,632 such messages in 731 witness files. Every RED in this repository has been printing a placeholder instead of its own cause.
think The fix is one function. do_assert stripped the quotes and printed the raw bytes, never calling interpolate. Now it tracks whether the reason was quoted and renders through assert_message: a quoted message interpolates like every other string, an unquoted reason shows exactly as written, and a message that cannot render falls back to its own raw text rather than replacing the failure with a second one. The assertion is the news; the reason must never swallow it.
think The fix paid for itself within the hour, and that is how the fifth red surfaced. The next suite run said "a per-rung witness went RED -- tools/caravan_arrange_witness.rish" and the rung was innocent: it runs caravan/bin/read, which caravan_read_witness alone builds, and which the roster sings after most of its borrowers. 36 of the 52 rungs borrow that binary. The whole arc has only ever been green on a tree an earlier run left warm.
think Closed that two ways rather than one. Each of the 36 now builds caravan/read.rye itself, so any rung runs alone on a cold tree; and the choir clears caravan/bin before it sings, which turns cold-start self-sufficiency from a property nobody measured into a fact this witness checks every run.
think Left REDS #91 open on purpose. Eleven active-designing documents name no Two Rooms room, and naming a room is a claim about the work rather than a formatting repair -- guessing eleven of them would put false claims in dated documents. The scan's own output is the list; the pass belongs to a design round.
obs The ledger crossed its own bound before the rows would fit -- 23,349 of 24,576 with three reds to book. Folded closed rows 80-87 to crux/archive/, the fifth such fold this ledger has taken, checking the living-pin guard roster first because REDS #87's whole lesson is that a rename breaks the guard that watches the pins. The header substring the roster matches was untouched.
obs Two of this round's reds were only visible because the other three had been closed. #89 made #92 legible; #88's diagnosis is what exposed #89. Reds compound in both directions, and the cheapest one to fix first was the one that made the others speak.
obs The honest correction to what I reported earlier: the Caravan molt's GREEN was real -- those binaries were built from molted sources in the same session -- yet the suite that reported it was not cold-start reproducible, and saying so plainly matters more than the reassurance.
obs Serializing the build makes the suite slower, and that cost is real rather than nominal. It is the right trade while a false RED can send a sound rung to the ledger; if the wall time becomes the binding constraint, per-run output trees are the answer, and that is a 145-file sweep to be planned rather than smuggled into a fix.
loom witness=glow_build_concurrency lanes=6 unguarded_fails=5 guarded_fails=0 answered=6 leftover_temps=0
loom rishi tests_pass=23 tests_fail=0 assert_messages_affected=1632 witness_files_affected=731
loom caravan borrowers_fixed=36 of_rungs=52 suite_start=cold cold_suite_rungs_green=52 cold_suite_exit=0
loom reds booked=5 closed=3 open=2 ledger_bytes=18585 bound=24576
file crux/REDS.md rows 88-92 booked; closed rows 80-87 folded to archive to bring the pin back under its bound
file tools/glow_run_worker.sh the two guards -- one bounded lock, one atomic rename
file tools/fixtures/glow_build_concurrency_scan.sh the experiment, its control generated from the worker so it cannot drift
file tools/glow_build_concurrency_witness.rish the standing proof, registered in the era suite so it is never unheard
file rishi/src/main.rye do_assert renders its reason through assert_message -- 1,632 RED messages across the tree stop printing placeholders
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish per-run roster lists, and the choir now clears caravan/bin so it sings from a cold tree
file nixos/configuration.nix time.timeZone seated -- the one line whose absence made this pier run UTC while declaring Eastern
recommend check-in (Claude) three reds closed on metal and two left open by choice. REDS #90 waits on a host act -- nixos/rebuild-outer.sh from outside the jail -- and closes when one_clock_witness runs GREEN afterwards. REDS #91 wants a design pass to name the room for eleven documents, which is a claim about the work rather than a repair. The open question this round raises on its own is whether the serialized build's wall time is acceptable, since the honest alternative is per-run output trees and that touches 145 files naming glow/.cache and glow/bin.
